{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/941026-back-to-school-gear-where-does-it-all-go","id":941026,"title":"Back to school gear. Where does it all go??","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-31T21:33:47-07:00","id":941026,"title":"Back to school gear. Where does it all go??","content":"This afternoon, while in both Meijer and Aldi, i got to chatting with 2 couples i saw in both spots, and both were doing 'back to school shopping' for their kids.. My discussion with the first couple, was over just how much pens, pencils, paper the kids seem to GO through in a school year, which is real surprising considering HOW much school work these days seems to be done on Tablets, PCs, Laptops, ipads etc...<br /> Then discussing with couple 2, it went into the # of backpacks kids go through.. Tearing them up, getting bored with 'that bag, i need a new one' (especially it seems with daughters)..<br /> One of the workers, shelf stocking, chimed in going on about how it was 'rare for her to even see their kids doodling on paper, spending so much time ON techie stuff..<br /> <br /> So where does it all go???<br /> <br /> I know as a kid going through the UK school system, even a box of 10 pens/10 pencils lasted me the entire year and usually i would have 3-4 left by school year's end.. Though i will admit i went through backpacks frequently cause i tossed them around a lot, and thus ripped the siding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T22:49:01-07:00","id":941047,"title":"","content":"As someone who until five years ago was a kid, I honestly don't know. I've always been extremely careful with my school supplies. But this is definitely a thing, I've seen and heard others complaining about it.<br /> <br /> Signed, certified former kid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T06:01:55-07:00","id":941146,"title":"","content":"Wear and tear. Backpacks fall apart due to weight of books, pens lose ink, pencils are ground down to nubs, either of them get lost. Some classes tend to have odd requirements, like to bring in certain brand of red, green and blue pens, which won't be used in any other classes.<br /> <br /> Even when more lengthy work is done on computers, in most schools everyday worksheets would be done with pen or pencil.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T07:34:14-07:00","id":941175,"title":"","content":"When I was a kid (after computers, but before laptops/tablets were common), I'd keep my Jansport backpack for a couple of years (until I got bored with it instead of it falling apart). My notebooks looked like a mess by the end of the year, but I didn't really need new ones. <br /> <br /> However, I did loose pens and pencils all the time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T09:05:55-07:00","id":941220,"title":"","content":"I had the same Jansport backpack from 7th grade until graduation, no idea about the backpacks. But pencils and pens fall into the abyss I'm pretty sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10575-lilappleblossom","name":"lilappleblossom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T09:36:33-07:00","id":941228,"title":"","content":"Kids lose supplies all the time. And then they borrow the stuff they need from friends who did not lose theirs... And then lose it. Pens get disassembled by bored kids and turned into spit wad shooters, or used to draw on someone's skin and the oil gunks up the ball point and it can't write any more, or they just get broken. Pencils get sharpened down to nothing, or the erasers get all weird and dried out and don't work any more (anyone know why that happens? I'm still not sure) and who wants a pencil with an eraser that doesn't work. Paper gets shoved down to the bottom of the backpack and crumpled under the weight of books, binders, laptops, and what ever else. Kids rip pages out of spiral notebooks to lend to friends who lost their paper, or to be turned into a teacher. And let me tell you, you rip one page out of one of those notebooks and it's only a matter of time before the whole thing falls apart. Something about the way they're bound makes them weirdly prone to this happening. Backpacks go through an unbelievable amount of wear, between the weight of all the stuff that gets kept in them and the way kids throw them around, yank on the back of someone else's, tug back and forth on them to try to steal someone's bag or keep your own. Plus, yeah, sometimes kids just want a new one because there's a whole backpack fashion culture.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T11:12:00-07:00","id":941274,"title":"","content":"On that eraser issue, one of the brands we used to get at the local woolworths in the UK&lt; seemed to get to a certain spot of use then it just crumbled like cold cheese..<br /> <br /> As for the spiral notebook, i have never seen that issue.. heck some of the ones i STILL have, have had many pages ripped out, but have not fallen apart.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T12:20:23-07:00","id":941334,"title":"","content":"Sorry, not spiral notebooks. Those are the good ones. I meant composition notebooks. You know, these things:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://www.dollartree.com/assets/product_images/styles/alternate_large/20585.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 08-01-2016, 03:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T14:41:40-07:00","id":941414,"title":"","content":"Again, i have had some of those which didn't fall apart just from taking some pages out.. Maybe the ones you have seen were poorly glued together..?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T14:56:11-07:00","id":941426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>garhkal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/941026-back-to-school-gear-where-does-it-all-go?p=941414#post941414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, i have had some of those which didn't fall apart just from taking some pages out.. Maybe the ones you have seen were poorly glued together..?</div> </div> </div> </div>They're usually sewn rather than glued, and the pages are essentially folded in half, such that the front and back page are actually the same piece of paper and the two closest to the center are actually the same piece of paper, etc. so if you rip a page out of it, it's counterpart will often fall out because the point you ripped one from is also the point where the other is sewn into the binding. And once they've both fallen out, the sewing is just a bit looser. It won't always cause the notebook to fall apart, but the the more pages you rip out, the greater risk there is for more pages to start falling out, and for the whole thing to eventually start to fall apart at the spine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T11:52:42-07:00","id":942133,"title":"","content":"Ah.. I think we are on about 2 different types of notepads..<br /> <br /> As a linked question.. Someone over on Classic battletech mentioned his kids going to elementary have to 'put all their supplies' into a &quot;Communal pool' that each kid takes from AS needed, so what you bought for your son/daughter, may NOT be what he winds up using in class..<br /> <br /> Anyone heard anything like that before?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T12:13:52-07:00","id":942142,"title":"","content":"I've heard of similar things, yes. Each school seems to be different about supplies, or at least there's no all-encompassing rule. Some have really strict guidelines, some don't. Sometimes an individual class might have specific requirements but the rest of the school doesn't. It's not unnatural at all. Parents or kids usually get a form explaining the requirements, theoretically if you didn't approve you could find another school or have them transferred to another class.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T12:25:27-07:00","id":942154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>garhkal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/941026-back-to-school-gear-where-does-it-all-go?p=942133#post942133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a linked question.. Someone over on Classic battletech mentioned his kids going to elementary have to 'put all their supplies' into a &quot;Communal pool' that each kid takes from AS needed, so what you bought for your son/daughter, may NOT be what he winds up using in class..<br /> <br /> Anyone heard anything like that before?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sometimes schools with a lot of low-income families will do that, to insure the kids who's parents can't afford the supplies they need can still have access to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T15:26:39-07:00","id":942274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/941026-back-to-school-gear-where-does-it-all-go?p=942154#post942154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sometimes schools with a lot of low-income families will do that, to insure the kids who's parents can't afford the supplies they need can still have access to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>So effectively they are socialists.. And do the parents of the other kids have the right to opt out, so what THEY are spending on their own kids doesn't get 'redistributed' to all the others?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T15:40:56-07:00","id":942282,"title":"","content":"Dude, if you're more worried about saving a couple bucks on school supplies than about kids from struggling families getting the opportunity to succeed in school, then your priorities are in the wrong place.<br /> <br /> But if it bothers you that much, just put your kids in a different school.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T15:46:55-07:00","id":942290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/941026-back-to-school-gear-where-does-it-all-go?p=942282#post942282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dude, if you're more worried about saving a couple bucks on school supplies than about kids from struggling families getting the opportunity to succeed in school, then your priorities are in the wrong place.<br /> <br /> But if it bothers you that much, just put your kids in a different school.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed, I'd rather give a couple bucks to make sure all these kids are properly outfitted to learn over the $20 I would save not doing that. Same thing goes with lunches, my county just passed something that gave all children access to free lunches, so many people flipped out over it. They did not care that the reason this passed was because a large amount of children were going hungry at school, nope their precious money was so much more important than these kids. I really don't understand the worship of money, but I've never had much of my own so maybe that's why.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10575-lilappleblossom","name":"lilappleblossom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T16:17:38-07:00","id":942305,"title":"","content":"I've also seen it done in places where teachers need control over things. As we've noted, school supplies sometimes get lost. Some teachers find a way to get around that is by not having said supplies leave the class.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, there are schools with students who have been known to attack other kids for their things. So sometimes a strict code of everyone getting the same thing, or everyone sharing everything, is used.<br /> <br /> In either case schools usually send home memos about just purchasing standard supplies and not spending 500 dollars on a pen you don't want anyone but your child to use. If someone has a problem with this they're free to take their child from school and homeschool them or send them to a private school of their choice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T21:33:46-07:00","id":942476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/941026-back-to-school-gear-where-does-it-all-go?p=942282#post942282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dude, if you're more worried about saving a couple bucks on school supplies than about kids from struggling families getting the opportunity to succeed in school, then your priorities are in the wrong place.<br /> <br /> But if it bothers you that much, just put your kids in a different school.</div> </div> </div> </div>Char.. I don't have kids, let alone kids going to school. What i found strange, is that something like that would even be allowed to happen in public schools. Especially when i have heard some of the schools that DO do that, still seem to find funds to fully outfit their sports teams, but can't spare anything to help out the less fortunate kids, so make everyone else's kid take that brunt..<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T21:53:34-07:00","id":942483,"title":"","content":"Outfitting an entire football team is several thousand dollars and usually done through extensive fundraising. Some schools have contracts with major sporting goods companies like Nike, or advertising from others, because their games bring in a lot of people. Most of that money goes back into sports or other extracurricular activities, like band.<br /> <br /> That's high school, though. And not every high school by a longshot.<br /> <br /> Elementary school sports, middle school sports, aren't usually getting all this money.<br /> <br /> As for why it's allowed to happen, teachers are generally only able to teach. When a parent can't pay to outfit their child, or doesn't care enough to ensure they have the required supplies, then the burden falls on the school and most schools can't equip every student. It's not uncommon for teachers to do it, bringing in extra supplies for those who they know won't have them.<br /> <br /> But in the end we're talking about pencils, pens, maybe a backpack, some notebooks. Calculator, maybe a flash drive. While classes that operate entirely on computers are more common now than they were in the 90s, they're still not everywhere. Usually when they do have classes like that there's also classroom or school-use tablets. You can also bring your own to school, I believe, if you have an issue with school-supplied devices. <a href=\"https://www.washingtonpost.com/local/education/tablets-proliferate-in-nations-classrooms-and-take-a-swipe-at-the-status-quo/2014/05/17/faa27ba4-dbbd-11e3-8009-71de85b9c527_story.html\" target=\"_blank\">There's an article about the shift to electronic devices, and the problems that can roadblock it, you can read here.</a><br /> <br /> Though, again, it's not something every school district could even pull off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-03-2016, 01:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T09:28:29-07:00","id":942759,"title":"","content":"On the kids gear thing, especially when it comes to technology, other factors come into play.<br /> <br /> If a school says &quot;you must have a PC laptop of X specifications&quot; then the first thing you're going to run into is the fact that most of the parents don't understand the requirements. They're going to go to an electronics store and say their kid needs a laptop for school.<br /> <br /> From that, some are going to try to upsell the parents on the most expensive and flashy bit of gear, using the pitch that it's needed or will help the child. Of course that means an expensive thing that's going to break in a year or two, if it's not stolen.<br /> <br /> Others are going to assume something completely different and sell them an apple instead of a PC, or the cool new tablet or whatever, which is going to be incompatible with the decades plus old software the school is using, making it useless.<br /> <br /> Still others are going to use the parents as a way to dump obsolete and outdated gear, generally at an inflated price.<br /> <br /> And that's just the price of the average level of unawareness of tech specs. You're also going to get the parents that KNOWINGLY buy the overpowered machines, can't afford anything but the third-hand decade old laptop, or have political or tech preferences that they will enforce upon their children (No child of mine is going to use a samsung product!)<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T10:10:12-07:00","id":942785,"title":"","content":"Well, I am from Georgia whose public school system, in my my opinion, isn't just a shit show, it's a shit show studio that routinely wins the shit show Oscars. For instance, one of my special education aides in middle school was a women was severely allergic to bananas, to the point where they burned her skin if she so much as touched them, which meant that I had to careful eating the lunches I brought from home. This eventually led to me having to get a new backpack because my old one had a banana explode in it, covering it in banana gunk and creating a health hazard for the poor lady (she was good at her job, don't get me wrong, and I was happy to accommodate her, but having buy a new backpack was still a pain).<br /> <br /> So that is one reason I had to buy a new backpack.<br /> <br /> Also there is the fact that standardized test are administered by the textbook companies, who have a nasty habit of making it so you can only get the answers to certain questions right if you have THEIR textbook, which is is part of why the poorer school do worse on tests. So a parent may very well wind up having to buy a different textbook than the one the school has to ensure their child can actually pass their tests.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigen